From 7a8a2da7a51c2beed0fa431f03a40d317508e830 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bill Hlavacek <bill.hlavacek@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:18:27 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] bngsim: throw instead of exit(1) where a BNG-written function
 cannot be built

NFsim called exit(1) when it could not build a function or a rule that
reads one, so a model NFsim cannot run killed the host process with no
message. BNG-written models reach these at load:

- A(b)%x + B(a)%y -> A(b!1).B(a!1) fA(x)*fB(y), with fA and fB reading
  Molecules observables: the rate law reads both reactants, which
  DORRxnClass does not support.
- The same rule with Species observables: a local function cannot read a
  Species observable, because SpeciesObservable::clone() was never written
  ("not yet updated ... fix me").
- fAB(x,y) = k*(1+SA(x))*(1+SB(y)) on that rule: a local function takes
  one argument (LocalFunction's constructor).
- g() = f() + k*SB: a function that calls another function cannot also
  read an observable (createCompositeFunction, whose return value
  createFunction ignores, so only a throw stops the load).

bngsim's Python process exited with code 1 during initialize() on each.
Throw std::runtime_error naming the function, rule or observable and the
reason, as carry 0005 did for six other files: every live exit(1) in
DORreaction.cpp and observable.cpp, LocalFunction's constructor checks
and its muParser failure in prepareForSimulation(), and the composite
check in parseFuncXML.cpp. NFinput::initReactionRules and
NFinput::initFunctions catch the load-time throws and fail the load, and
bngsim's prepare_system turns a prepareForSimulation() throw into an
error, so the host reports each. The internal-error paths at run time
(Observable::subtract, rate-factor changes on a non-DOR reactant) now
raise rather than exit. The ReactionClass destructor that runs when a
DOR constructor throws frees only arrays the base constructor has
already allocated. (bngsim issue #854 review)
